    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start. To help my students really get the impact, could you give them a few specific historical examples of landmark cases where substantive due process was used to secure these rights? It would be great if you could highlight how these rulings fundamentally changed the landscape for civil rights in America.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A key example is *Griswold v. Connecticut*, which established a constitutional right to privacy, protecting intimate decisions from government intrusion. In *Roe v. Wade*, the right to privacy, rooted in due process, was used to protect a woman's right to choose. Another important case is *Obergefell v. Hodges*, which used due process principles to guarantee the right to same-sex marriage nationwide. These rulings fundamentally expanded the scope of individual liberty beyond the explicitly listed rights in the Constitution.",
      "source": "target",
